# Level Design Document Contract

This is a binding process contract for **Level Blueprints** (full layout concepts) and **Level Concepts** (interactive environment concept sheets). Follow it exactly and consistently across every deliverable. Do not silently deviate from any rule below — if a source reference cannot satisfy a rule as-is, flag it explicitly rather than improvising.

## 0. Process Gate (Non-Negotiable)

Every deliverable follows two phases. **Do not generate images during the conversation phase.**

### Phase 1 — Conversation
1. Re-read this contract in full.
2. Re-read the pinned reference document(s) for the target doc type (blueprint or concept).
3. Produce a **Content Spec** (text only): zones/panels, copy, legend items, boss/goal, asset callouts.
4. User approves or edits the Content Spec. No image generation until approved.

### Phase 2 — Execution
1. Re-read this contract in full.
2. Generate the image using the approved Content Spec + pinned reference images.
3. Run the QA checklist for that doc type (Section 6). Fail = revise spec or regenerate; do not hand off a failing doc.
4. Save output to the path in Section 7.
5. User review. Revisions restart at Phase 1 (spec edit first).

