## 3. Level Concept Contract

Extracted from Level 2, 4, and 5 concept references. All new concepts (Levels 1, 3, 6) must match this template.

### 3.1 Canvas and framing
- **Format:** Portrait or square technical sheet on dark navy/grid background.
- **Layout:** Header + **2×2 panel grid** + footer. No full-level panorama.

### 3.2 Header (fixed structure)
- `TRASH DASH` logo (top-left).
- Center title block:
  - `TRASH DASH - LEVEL {N}` (level number may use accent color per refs)
  - `INTERACTIVE ENVIRONMENT CONCEPTS`
  - Stage subtitle line, e.g. `— SECRET SPACE CENTER STAGE —` or themed bar (Level 5 pattern)
- Optional top-right callout: pinned note or star badge with 1–3 design pillars (from Content Spec).

### 3.3 Four panels (fixed titles — subtitles are level-specific)

| # | Panel title (fixed) | Subtitle (level-specific, from spec) |
|---|---------------------|--------------------------------------|
| 1 | MAIN GROUND LANE | Primary walk surface for this level |
| 2 | RAISED PLATFORM / STEP-UP | Vertical step / retaining structure |
| 3 | SECONDARY PLATFORM | Elevated or supported secondary deck |
| 4 | FALL-GAP HAZARD | This level's hazard type (water, reactor pit, cosmic sludge, etc.) |

Each panel includes:
- **Number badge** — blue square, white numeral (top-left of panel)
- **Panel title** — ALL CAPS, bold
- **Subtitle** — mixed case, descriptive
- **Illustration** — painted side-view scene using **that level's terrain and foreground assets**
- **Four-layer depth legend** below the art:

| Layer | Label variants across refs | Purpose |
|-------|---------------------------|---------|
| Playable ground | FOREGROUND / PLAYABLE GROUND / Foreground (Playable) | Stand/jump surfaces |
| Close BG | CLOSE BACKGROUND | Near parallax props |
| Mid BG | MID BACKGROUND | Structural/environment mid layer |
| Distant BG | DISTANT BACKGROUND | Skyline / far parallax |

Each layer lists specific assets visible at that depth (from Content Spec).

### 3.4 Footer (fixed structure, level-specific content)
- **Design notes** — 3–4 bullet points (grounded surfaces, readable gameplay, parallax, level mood).
- **Material / theme icon row** — 4–5 circular or square icons drawn from that level's asset set with ALL CAPS labels.
- **Tagline** — level-specific slogan (e.g. Level 4 tape: `KEEP IT CLEAN.. DASH IT MEAN.`; Level 5: `KEEP SPACE CLEAN(ISH)`).
- Level 5 reference also includes a **color palette swatch row** — include when spec calls for it (space/industrial levels).

### 3.5 Level concept non-negotiables
- Exactly four panels in 2×2 grid — do not add or remove panels.
- Panel titles in Section 3.3 are fixed; only subtitles and illustrations change.
- Use level-specific assets only (from `output/level{N}/` manifest).
- Match the dark technical grid background and blue framing of Level 4/5 refs; Level 2 ref is the lighter suburban-night variant — **use Level 4/5 grid style as default** unless spec calls for suburban-night treatment (Level 1, Level 2 tone).

